\paragraph{Scoring window}
The historical deterministic regression gates and Table~\ref{tab:sim_results_rms_dir_basic}
use a trailing window $T_{\mathrm{RMS}}=60$~s.  The statistically powered
validation protocol instead uses the final \SI{900}{s} of each \SI{1200}{s}
run as its primary score, thereby excluding startup while retaining a long
steady-state record.  The runner reports per-axis and 3D displacement RMS,
roll/pitch/yaw RMS, bias errors, and diagnostic tuning variables
$(f,\tau,\sigma_{aw},r_S)$.

\paragraph{Paired Monte Carlo and adaptation ablations}
Ten predeclared repetitions independently vary wave phase, IMU noise and random
walk, and residual-error initialization.  Each seed triplet is shared by OU--II
and OU--III and by all ablations.  Phase surrogates apply a common random Fourier
phase at each frequency to the world-motion and attitude channels, preserving
their auto- and cross-spectra; body-frame specific force, angular rate, and
quaternion are subsequently reconstructed for kinematic consistency.  Results
are summarized by the sample mean and standard deviation, normal and bootstrap
95\% confidence intervals, and paired mean differences with Cohen's $d_z$ and
Hedges' $g_z$.

The adaptation study compares the online \emph{Adaptive} filter with
\emph{FixedNominal}, held at the noise-free operating point of the
$H_s=\SI{1.5}{m}$, $T_p=\SI{5.7}{s}$ sea, and \emph{FixedOracle}, held at the
known operating point of each stationary sea.  A non-stationary realization
uses a smooth transition from $(H_s,T_p)=(\SI{1.5}{m},\SI{5.7}{s})$ to
$(\SI{4.0}{m},\SI{11.4}{s})$ over $t=420$--$780$~s.  Its FixedOracle baseline
is fixed at the known final-sea point and is therefore a clairvoyant endpoint
reference rather than a deployable online method.  Machine-readable raw data,
statistics, seed manifests, LaTeX tables, and plots are generated by
\texttt{tools/ou\_validation.py}.  The completed full-protocol results are
reported in Sec.~\ref{sec:observer-comparison}; the versioned raw rows,
summaries, paired effects, and manifest are retained with the source tree.

